WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.040
After 16,000 plus paper checks, Google opens deep review publicly. This is MAG 7 Daily, episode 25. Google

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:13.300
research scientists Rajesh Jairam and Vincent Cohen Adad are taking the old paper assistant

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:18.780
tool out of private pilots and putting deep review in front of anyone. Opted in authors

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:29.640
is already got pre-submission notes on manuscripts at STOC 2026, ICML 2026, NURRIPS 2026, and ICLR 2027.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:35.160
The public system checks whether an argument holds together, test mathematical statements,

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.700
suggest edits, grounds, facts, and lines a document up against work that already exists.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.300
Launch inputs are PDFs and plain text, and multi-file uploads are still on the way.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:51.060
A Gemini API key raises the cap and opens the Deep Review API.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:56.580
Google Research says uploaded files are never used to train, fine-tune, or improve its

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.000
models.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.240
And the pilot write-up is the manuscript towards automating scientific review with Google's

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.320
paper assistant tool.

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:08.996
Apple told the Financial Times that iPhone Duo demand has been nothing short of extraordinary,

00:01:09.456 --> 00:01:12.636
and that it is working hard to get the phone into customers' hands.

00:01:12.636 --> 00:01:18.916
pre-orders opened at 5 in the morning Pacific on October 16th. Within minutes delivery dates

00:01:18.916 --> 00:01:25.196
moved from October 23rd to November, and by 5.30 they had reached January 25th. Apple

00:01:25.196 --> 00:01:31.856
no longer has a 2026 delivery slot, so a new order waits until early 2027, while those

00:01:31.856 --> 00:01:41.416
first orders are still due on October 23rd. MacRumors puts the price at $1,999. Up to $3,1999

00:01:41.416 --> 00:01:46.736
dollars for two terabytes, and the financial times framed it as the $2,000 duo slipping

00:01:46.736 --> 00:01:48.556
to 2027 within hours.

00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:55.149
Microsoft President and Vice Chairman Brad Smith, on October 16, launched co-pilot for

00:01:55.149 --> 00:01:59.129
legal with more than 20 specialized skills for commercial customers worldwide.

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:05.069
The skills ship as plug-ins, each tied to a job such as drafting a contract, reviewing

00:02:05.069 --> 00:02:08.769
an agreement, tracking obligations, or building a case timeline.

00:02:08.769 --> 00:02:15.029
Microsoft says the work lives mainly in desktop word and in co-work, which can pull obligations,

00:02:15.449 --> 00:02:20.429
deadlines, and trigger conditions out of contracts, emails, minutes, and other documents,

00:02:20.929 --> 00:02:24.909
compare terms across agreements, and turn a meeting into minutes and resolutions.

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:31.869
Named partner plugins include Bloomberg Law, Thompson Reuters High Q, DocuSign, Harvey,

00:02:31.869 --> 00:02:38.429
be, relativity, eye-manage, and net documents, spanning research, document management, e-signatures,

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:40.849
e-discovery, and transaction management.

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:46.369
The plugin registry rollout is gradual, and what you actually get can change with region,

00:02:46.729 --> 00:02:48.509
license, and administrator settings.

00:02:49.149 --> 00:02:54.889
Microsoft says the tool assists and does not replace legal judgment, so citations and suggested

00:02:54.889 --> 00:03:01.009
revisions still need a human check, and the buyer needs a commercial Microsoft 365 co-pilot

00:03:01.009 --> 00:03:07.189
license, plus a supported word setup. Apple has rewritten App Store rules so they explicitly

00:03:07.189 --> 00:03:13.169
cover AI-generated intimate images made without consent. Sexually explicit content was already

00:03:13.169 --> 00:03:19.209
banned. Developers now have to prevent and remove AI deepfakes themselves, and an app can come

00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:27.349
down if they do not. Guideline 1.2 names AI content creation apps. Guideline 2.5.19 says a feature

00:03:27.349 --> 00:03:32.469
that was not in the reviewed build can get the app, and the developer removed, which

00:03:32.469 --> 00:03:36.209
is aimed at notified tools that hit that function until after approval.

00:03:36.809 --> 00:03:42.449
The ban on apps that facilitate human trafficking or child exploitation now also covers alternative

00:03:42.449 --> 00:03:43.189
distribution.

00:03:44.009 --> 00:03:49.569
MacRumors says Apple warned XAI earlier this year that Grock would be pulled if new deepfakes

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:50.169
continued.

00:03:50.669 --> 00:03:53.969
XAI added safeguards, and an updated app was approved.

00:03:53.969 --> 00:03:59.809
The Verge adds that Apple did not remove X or GROC after users on X used GROC to make

00:03:59.809 --> 00:04:03.569
non-consensual, sexualized deepfakes, including of minors.

00:04:04.619 --> 00:04:10.219
Amazon's B Frontier and B Eclipse are drawing a bystander objection from Jeff Williams, a

00:04:10.219 --> 00:04:15.859
former AWS security engineer who is now Chief Information Security Officer at Sigma 360.

00:04:16.879 --> 00:04:21.079
GeekWire reports that the consent prompt and the indicator light reach the person wearing

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:27.039
the device, not the people being recorded. Amazon pointed to automatic shutoff and to reminders

00:04:27.039 --> 00:04:33.059
that tell the wearer to ask permission. Google Research counts more than 74,000 submissions

00:04:33.059 --> 00:04:44.519
this year to ICLR, NURRIPS and ICML, against about 45,000 in 2025, 32,000 in 2024, and 23,000 in 2023.

00:04:45.039 --> 00:04:50.799
Every user still gets two free document reviews a week. Pilot feedback stayed completely outside

00:04:50.799 --> 00:04:56.219
the official conference decision. And those papers were deleted promptly. The public product

00:04:56.219 --> 00:05:01.899
keeps an upload for one year so it can be shown again in the interface. Consistency checks are the

00:05:01.899 --> 00:05:08.279
machine's job. Higher-level judgment stays with people. Britain's competition watchdog already has

00:05:08.279 --> 00:05:15.459
Google and Amazon enaboring files, and on October 16th it proposed strategic market status for Microsoft's

00:05:15.459 --> 00:05:19.219
business software. The investigation that led there opened in May

00:05:19.219 --> 00:05:25.359
2026. The label does not find or assume wrongdoing. It is a gateway into the digital

00:05:25.359 --> 00:05:30.439
markets regime, and it could lead to rules on how Excel, Teams, and Copilot are

00:05:30.439 --> 00:05:35.159
bundled. Last year, the same authority designated Google in general search and

00:05:35.159 --> 00:05:40.479
an advertising, after finding the legal criteria met. In March, it started asking

00:05:40.479 --> 00:05:44.459
whether Amazon Web Services and Microsoft had followed through on commitments

00:05:44.459 --> 00:05:48.579
to widen customer choice and cloud, and whether more action was needed.

00:05:49.199 --> 00:05:54.459
The CMA says Microsoft has been dominant in UK business software for decades, from

00:05:54.459 --> 00:05:59.819
operating systems and productivity tools into cyber security and databases, and now into

00:05:59.819 --> 00:06:01.559
AI products and cloud services.

00:06:02.239 --> 00:06:07.459
Buying several products from one supplier can help UK businesses and public bodies, and

00:06:07.459 --> 00:06:11.759
switching can still be hard, because the stack is more seamless than a mix of vendors.

00:06:11.759 --> 00:06:11.959
controllers.

00:06:12.499 --> 00:06:17.739
Control of key APIs, technical interfaces, and data flows can stop arrival from matching

00:06:17.739 --> 00:06:18.399
that function.

00:06:19.079 --> 00:06:23.879
The questions on the table are whether customers can pick their own AI tools, whether anyone

00:06:23.879 --> 00:06:29.039
can compete with co-pilot, whether security bundles narrowed choice, and whether licensing

00:06:29.039 --> 00:06:30.319
shaped cloud options.

00:06:31.059 --> 00:06:36.399
Sarah Cardell, the CMA's chief executive, said organizations should be able to choose what

00:06:36.399 --> 00:06:39.439
works, switch when they want, and combine suppliers.

00:06:39.439 --> 00:06:45.999
A Microsoft spokesperson told Reuters the products, including co-pilot, are open and interoperable,

00:06:46.359 --> 00:06:49.019
so customers can use them beside competing services.

00:06:49.699 --> 00:06:52.239
Microsoft did not immediately answer Benzinga.

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:58.994
Benzinga says Analysts highlight 30 million co-pilot seats, Azure Momentum, and Maya 300

00:06:58.994 --> 00:07:02.614
inference chips ahead of fiscal first quarter 2027 results.

00:07:03.254 --> 00:07:07.674
That seat count is the Analysts highlight, not a figure Microsoft gave the regulator.

00:07:07.674 --> 00:07:12.374
Comments on the proposed decision are invited by November 13th.

00:07:12.414 --> 00:07:17.434
On the calendar, Apple's October 15th newsroom release still says iPhone Duo availability

00:07:17.434 --> 00:07:19.254
begins on October 30th.

00:07:19.674 --> 00:07:24.574
The same pre-order page tells buyers to check back on October 24th for in-store pickup.

00:07:25.114 --> 00:07:30.394
Before we go, the competition and market authorities final decision on that Microsoft designation

00:07:30.394 --> 00:07:32.854
is due February 13th, 2027.

00:07:33.594 --> 00:07:35.174
That's Mag 7 Daily for today.

